So here I was with one of the most promising Samurai I'd played in
quite some time, thanks to a few striking turns of luck.

1) a *ludicrous* number of ?oEA on DL1/2/3 (like 6)
2) cleaned out a scroll shop on DL 4, netting 2 u?oID and 1 b?oID, 3
u?oEA and a u?oGenocide (which I used to nuke giant eels, the bane of
my existence), and a /ton/ of zorkmids. (plus a few ?oFire,
?oPunishment and ?oAmnesia, which I sold in Minetown)
3) An armor shop on DL5 which netted me an elven broadsword, a dwarvish
mithril-coat, a cloak of displacement, blessed +3 kicking boots and
gauntlets of dexterity
4) a helpful goblin which dropped a +4 orcish helm
5) a wand of polymorph which let me turn my little dog into a blue
dragon
6) a magic whistle

I thought things were looking pretty good, so I headed into the Mines,
looking to buy some protection, candles and hopefully scrolls, and
maybe luck out and hit into something else. Still no ?oEW yet, so my
katana was still +0 and was corroded due to a stupid move with acid
blobs.  On a lark I decided to train broadsword to basic, and
discovered it was dicing things up pretty nicely, so I wasted a ?oID to
see what it was - +4 out of the box, nice. On my way to minetown I got
ambushed by an orc horde shortly after escaping a rather hairy
encounter with a gnome with a wand of cold who got me good, so I #named
my broadsword Orcrist, and proceeded to massacre the offending orcs.
Tons of scimitars and a pretty good pile of zorkmids was my reward, so
down to Minetown I went. Cue one hairy moment where my pet tried to eat
Izchak, promptly cured with my /oTeleportation, last charge
unfortunately. Robbed the remaining shops blind, except the general
store where I sold a ton of junk. Bought 5 points of protection (alas,
not more - I was XL 10 by now), let my pet grease the watch captain and
scored a long sword, to be turned into Excalibur later unless I get
something better first. So, down I went to Mine's End, and all was well
until I stepped on a teleport trap!

    Next thing I know, I'm surrounded by vampires and mummies and
floating eyes. I narrowly survive this battle with much E-wording,
running and shooting, even though my pet is there doing even more
damage than me! I had to pray for healing once, too. The final move of
the battle killed a floating eye which left a corpse (on the same
square as one I'd killed earlier in the fight, though ISTR that didn't
leave a corpse). I didn't have telepathy yet so I sauntered over, ate
the corpse, and... Ulch! That meat was tainted!

     Well, crap. I pray. Now Amaterasu is pissed off at me, and I'm
still sick. Double crap. I know 'Cure Sickness' but it's at 100%
failure. I take off all my armor, it's still at 100%. So I quaff an
un-IDed potion in desperation. It's paralysis, and I die of food
poisoning with my feet frozen to the floor. GAAAAH! Crap!

     It was an annoying way to die, especially on a a character who was
otherwise doing so well, but I still have to wonder how that corpse got
tainted so fast. Maybe that first e did leave a corpse and I ate that,
but I really could have sworn there was no corpse on that square before
the second e moved there, and there was only one afterward. The only
thing I had in my inventory that it strikes me I should have tried
before un-IDed potions, was a /oPolymorph. Does polyselfing cure
sickness?



